{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The RNA-only pipeline is now well-characterized: scvi_n200 is the clear best encoder (config_004 vs 001, config_008), multiprofile+avgpool gives the largest single gain (+13pp, config_005), and transformer aggregation adds nothing over avgpool (config_006). The current best is ~0.65 accuracy. The biggest remaining uncertainty is the multimodal fusion axis, which is completely untested. Image alone (ResNet50, config_010) is very weak (0.208), so it is genuinely uncertain whether image features add complementary signal or merely noise when fused with the strong RNA representation. Config_030 takes the proven best RNA pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and adds ResNet50 image features with the simplest possible fusion (concat), changing only the modality/fusion axis. This directly answers whether the image modality contributes any incremental value above the 0.65 RNA-only ceiling. If concat helps, weighted fusion and ViT encoders become natural follow-ups; if it does not, we avoid wasting budget on the full 24-config multimodal grid. This is the highest-information experiment under the remaining budget because it resolves the single largest open design question with a minimal, interpretable change."
}

